<title>USA: State Bank of Long Island wins N. Hempstead, N.Y.</title>
<headline>State Bank of Long Island wins N. Hempstead, N.Y.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State Bank of Long Island said it won $18.3 million of North Hempstead, N.Y., bond anticipation notes (BANs) 1997, Series A.</p>
<p>The bank won the BANs in three parts. A $5 miilion portion had a 4 percent coupon; another $5 million portion had a 4 percent coupon; and an $8.3 million portion had a 4 percent coupon.</p>
<p>The net interest rate average for the offering was 3.7463 percent.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
